{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"vinyl-dubnium-squamata","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nWhen an egress proxy refuses a gate LLM request by policy, the failure classifier labels it \"Transient connection blip — retry immediately\" (RETRY_NOW, exit 11). Retrying cannot succeed: the refusal is a fixed proxy policy, not a blip.\n\nObserved 2026-11-22 21:44 PST: `review-plan antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow` run inside the Claude Code Bash sandbox without `api.anthropic.com` in the command's allowed hosts returned INDETERMINATE with `llm-degrade: RETRY_NOW — Transient connection blip`. The FallbackModel sub-exceptions, captured by wrapping `run_failure.interpret_failure` around a single-turn `get_runner(resolve_gate_config(\".\")).run(...)` call, were for both candidates: `ModelAPIError(Connection error.) <- anthropic.APIConnectionError <- httpx.ProxyError(\"403 not in this command's allowed_domains ...\") <- httpcore.ProxyError`. The same probe with `api.anthropic.com` allowed returned a completion. So the LLM transport does route through the proxy (the c8118c62e81 fix works); only the classification is wrong.\n\nCause in code: `src/rebar/llm/failure.py::_map` has no arm for `httpx.ProxyError`; the wrapped `ModelAPIError` without a status code falls to the final `ModelAPIError -> RETRY_NOW` arm, and the fallback-group classifier lets any retryable leg win.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A gate LLM failure whose cause chain holds an `httpx.ProxyError` from a proxy refusal (CONNECT answered with a 4xx) is not classified RETRY_NOW or WAIT_AND_RETRY, and its surfaced message names the proxy refusal.\n- [ ] A unit test builds that cause chain (ModelAPIError <- APIConnectionError <- httpx.ProxyError 403) inside a FallbackExceptionGroup and asserts the non-retryable class; existing ConnectError/ConnectTimeout cases keep RETRY_NOW.","id":"f8d9-1d45-f3f4-4ab7","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Proxy policy refusal of a gate LLM call is classified as a transient blip"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795413052009540001,"uuid":"de1bd006-3a26-4c2c-a8d8-ae33b25bd331"}